    "bodyDocument": {
      "textSnapshot": "Problem:\nSearch ranking degrades when prose queries use different word forms than code identifiers. Specifically:\n\"logs a user in\" (split across tokens) failed to find the login identifier because the verb was separated from its particle.\n\"authentication\" (full spelling) matched none of the auth-named functions, returning wrong results.\nSubstring matching caused false positives: \"login\" substring appeared in unrelated identifiers like runLogging, leading to incorrect ranking.\n\"write the log in json format\" incorrectly matched login functions instead of logging ones.\nSolution:\nFour targeted fixes to query term extraction and name-based ranking:\nTokenized name matching: Replaced raw substring search with token-boundary matching in searchNameTokenMatchesTerm, so \"log\" only matches the log token, not a substring of login. Restores the ability to distinguish login from logging identifiers.\nSeparable phrasal verb recovery: Added searchCompoundJoins to detect phrasal verbs split by their objects in prose—\"logs a user in\" now recovers the joined term login by scanning for patterns up to 3 tokens apart. Determiner and object-head checks prevent false positives (\"write the log in JSON\" stays excluded).\nAbbreviation table and alias expansion: Introduced searchTermAbbreviations mapping 48 common prose spellings to code abbreviations (authentication→auth, configuration→config, etc.). These aliases enter the query at retrieval time via BM25 preprocessing, ensuring auth-related functions surface even when the prose never says \"auth\". Word variants searchNameWordVariants handle plurals and inflections on both sides of comparisons.\nOffline retrieval evaluation: New test corpus (search_eval_test.go) with five cases pinning the specific regressions—separated phrasal verbs, prose abbreviations, noun+preposition false positives, and name-coverage saturation—to prevent future reintroduction.\nThese changes are additive: split spellings and original terms stay in queries alongside joined and abbreviated forms. Measured on entireio/cli, \"authentication\" now scores auth functions and compound phrasal verbs route correctly to their joined forms.",
      "etag": "W/\"2026-09-10T14:10:13.77407Z\""
    }
  }
}
"}

